Role of OLAP
OLAP (Online Analytical Processing) is used to analyse large amounts of order data from many
angles. Orders are viewed along dimensions such as product, customer and time, and measures such
as Total_Amount are summed.
 - Roll-up: summarise to a higher level (product totals to category totals, or daily orders to monthly
   orders).
 - Drill-down: go from totals to detail (from yearly order totals down to month, then to a single
   order).
 - Slice and dice: pick one value or a sub-cube of the data (only Laptop orders (slice), or Laptop and
   Mouse orders in two months (dice)).
 - Pivot: rotate the view to compare two dimensions side by side.
 - OLAP gives fast answers on large historical data, so decision makers can see trends without
   writing complex queries.
Conclusion: simple SQL (SELECT, aggregate functions, GROUP BY) gives the required reports,
and OLAP lets us analyse the same data from many angles.


