Q. 8. Write minimum 10 complex queries on MongoDB collections using different
keywords, comparison operators and logical operators.
Collection used: library.books (7 documents inserted in Q3). Start with: use library

Query 1: Comparison $gt: books costing more than 450
  db.books.find(
    { price: { $gt: 450 } },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, price: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Database System Concepts', price: 650 }
  { title: 'Python Crash Course', price: 500 }
  { title: 'Clean Code', price: 550 }

Query 2: $gte and $lte together: price from 300 to 500
  db.books.find(
    { price: { $gte: 300, $lte: 500 } },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, price: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Learning SQL', price: 450 }
  { title: 'Python Crash Course', price: 500 }
  { title: 'Wings of Fire', price: 300 }
  { title: 'MongoDB Basics', price: 400 }

Query 3: $in: category is Database or Fiction
  db.books.find(
    { category: { $in: ['Database', 'Fiction'] } },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, category: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Database System Concepts', category: 'Database' }
  { title: 'Learning SQL', category: 'Database' }
  { title: 'The Alchemist', category: 'Fiction' }
  { title: 'MongoDB Basics', category: 'Database' }

Query 4: Logical $or: Fiction books or books cheaper than 400
  db.books.find(
    { $or: [ { category: 'Fiction' }, { price: { $lt: 400 } } ] },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, category: 1, price: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'The Alchemist', category: 'Fiction', price: 250 }
  { title: 'Wings of Fire', category: 'Biography', price: 300 }

Query 5: Logical $and: Database books costing more than 400
  db.books.find(
    { $and: [ { category: 'Database' }, { price: { $gt: 400 } } ] },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, price: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Database System Concepts', price: 650 }
  { title: 'Learning SQL', price: 450 }

Query 6: Logical $nor: neither Database nor Programming
  db.books.find(
    { $nor: [ { category: 'Database' }, { category: 'Programming' } ] },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, category: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'The Alchemist', category: 'Fiction' }
  { title: 'Wings of Fire', category: 'Biography' }

Query 7: $exists: books that have a rating field
  db.books.find(
    { rating: { $exists: true } },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, rating: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Database System Concepts', rating: 4.5 }
  { title: 'Learning SQL', rating: 4.2 }
  { title: 'The Alchemist', rating: 4.0 }

Query 8: Nested field with dot notation: publisher city is Mumbai
  db.books.find(
    { 'publisher.city': 'Mumbai' },
    { _id: 0, title: 1, publisher: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Learning SQL', publisher: { name: 'Shroff', city: 'Mumbai' } }
  { title: 'MongoDB Basics', publisher: { name: 'Shroff', city: 'Mumbai' } }

Query 9: $regex: titles starting with a letter from A to L
  db.books.find(
    { title: { $regex: '^[A-L]' } },
    { _id: 0, title: 1 }
  )

Output:
  { title: 'Database System Concepts' }
  { title: 'Learning SQL' }
  { title: 'Clean Code' }

Query 10: sort() and limit(): top 3 costliest books
  db.books.find({}, { _id: 0, title: 1, price: 1 })
    .sort({ price: -1 })
    .limit(3)

Output:
  { title: 'Database System Concepts', price: 650 }
  { title: 'Clean Code', price: 550 }
  { title: 'Python Crash Course', price: 500 }

Query 11: countDocuments(): number of Database books
  db.books.countDocuments({ category: 'Database' })

Output:
  3

Query 12: Aggregation $group: average price per category
  db.books.aggregate([
    { $group: { _id: '$category', avgPrice: { $avg: '$price' } } },
    { $sort: { _id: 1 } }
  ])

Output:
  { _id: 'Biography', avgPrice: 300.0 }
  { _id: 'Database', avgPrice: 500.0 }
  { _id: 'Fiction', avgPrice: 250.0 }
  { _id: 'Programming', avgPrice: 525.0 }

Conclusion: MongoDB supports comparison ($gt, $gte, $lt, $lte, $in), logical ($and, $or, $nor),
element ($exists), regex, nested-field, sort/limit and aggregation operators for flexible querying.


